IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `plan55-nouns`
IMPORT `plan55-cross-references`

-- Row il-55. The three controls point at what they say, the two second readings are recorded as what they are, each limb of each reading says where it was read from,
-- and the recorded facts about the defects are what NOTES.md says they are.
-- The defects themselves are NOT asserted sound anywhere in this file: their six failing assertions are in plan55-tests-xrefs-red.l4.
-- Every expected value is written from the texts quoted in plan55-cross-references.l4, not from the output of the module.

§ `Tests of the controls`

-- Control A (the objection in section 152(א2)), control B (the enacting formula's section 145א) and control C/D (the list of arbitrator appraisers, section 202ג): the citing words and the target are described alike.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: s 145ב(ב)(9), the citation of s 152(א2)`)
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: the enacting formula of the licensing regulations to s 145א`)
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: arbitrator definition to s 202ג`)
-- None of the controls has a target that is missing or repealed.
#ASSERT (NOT ((`reference: s 145ב(ב)(9), the citation of s 152(א2)`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `a paragraph (4) of subsection (א2) of section 145, which the consolidation does not print: it prints that subsection as one sentence with no paragraphs`))
#ASSERT (NOT ((`reference: the enacting formula of the licensing regulations to s 145א`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `a section of the Law that was repealed, so that the section prints no text`))
#ASSERT (NOT ((`reference: arbitrator definition to s 202ג`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `no section 198א of the Law: the consolidation prints no section with that number`))

§ `Tests of the two second readings`

-- Reading B of the respondent definition (198א read as 198(א)) and reading B of regulation 2(ד) (202(ה)(2) read as 202ה(2)) are supplied by this row. The two descriptions agree under each,
-- which says what the reading would be and does not say that either reading is the one meant (forks F4 and F5 in NOTES.md).
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: respondent definition, read as s 198(א)`)
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: reg 2(ד) of the pay regulations, read as s 202ה(2)`)
#ASSERT (`reference: respondent definition, read as s 198(א)`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `a reading supplied by this row; no page prints it`
#ASSERT (`reference: reg 2(ד) of the pay regulations, read as s 202ה(2)`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `a reading supplied by this row; no page prints it`
#ASSERT (`reference: respondent definition, read as s 198(א)`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `the definition of the respondent in subsection (א) of section 198 of the Law`
#ASSERT (`reference: reg 2(ד) of the pay regulations, read as s 202ה(2)`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `paragraph (2) of section 202ה of the Law, a condition of qualification to serve as an arbitrator appraiser`

§ `Tests of what was read from where`

-- No citation here has both limbs read from the official instruments alone: the target of each is the consolidation or rests on it for what came after the page read, and the second readings are supplied.
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: s 145ב(ב)(7)(א), first citation, to s 145(א2)(4)`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: s 145ב(ב)(7)(א), second citation, to s 145(א3)(4)`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: s 145ב(ב)(9), the citation of s 152(א2)`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: reg 83(א) of the licensing regulations to s 257א`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: the enacting formula of the licensing regulations to s 145א`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: respondent definition, as printed, to s 198א`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: respondent definition, read as s 198(א)`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: arbitrator definition to s 202ג`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: reg 2(ד) of the pay regulations, as printed, to s 202(ה)(2)`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: reg 2(ד) of the pay regulations, read as s 202ה(2)`))
-- Defect A (both citations) and control A: limb (a) is the consolidation only; limb (b) is the words as published on the page image of Sefer HaChukim 2450 p. 510.
#ASSERT (`reference: s 145ב(ב)(7)(א), first citation, to s 145(א2)(4)`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 145ב(ב)(7)(א), first citation, to s 145(א2)(4)`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official page image of the words as published; that no later instrument touched them is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 145ב(ב)(7)(א), second citation, to s 145(א3)(4)`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 145ב(ב)(7)(א), second citation, to s 145(א3)(4)`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official page image of the words as published; that no later instrument touched them is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 145ב(ב)(9), the citation of s 152(א2)`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 145ב(ב)(9), the citation of s 152(א2)`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official page image of the words as published; that no later instrument touched them is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
