§ `Tests of what the two descriptions of the defects say`

-- What the citing words say it points at, and what the target is, as the texts show them.
#ASSERT (`reference: s 145ב(ב)(7)(א), first citation, to s 145(א2)(4)`)'s `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS `a provision of section 145 under which an application becomes absorbed`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 145ב(ב)(7)(א), first citation, to s 145(א2)(4)`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `a paragraph (4) of subsection (א2) of section 145, which the consolidation does not print: it prints that subsection as one sentence with no paragraphs`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 145ב(ב)(7)(א), second citation, to s 145(א3)(4)`)'s `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS `the Minister's setting of the preconditions for absorbing an application`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 145ב(ב)(7)(א), second citation, to s 145(א3)(4)`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `the treating of an application as absorbed when the engineer gives no notice within the Minister's period, which is what paragraph (4) of subsection (א3) of section 145 prints`
#ASSERT (`reference: reg 83(א) of the licensing regulations to s 257א`)'s `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS `a section of the Law under which inspectors are authorised, whose wording this row did not read`
#ASSERT (`reference: reg 83(א) of the licensing regulations to s 257א`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `a section of the Law that was repealed, so that the section prints no text`
#ASSERT (`reference: respondent definition, as printed, to s 198א`)'s `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS `a definition of the respondent in a section 198א of the Law`
#ASSERT (`reference: respondent definition, as printed, to s 198א`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `no section 198א of the Law: the consolidation prints no section with that number`
#ASSERT (`reference: reg 2(ד) of the pay regulations, as printed, to s 202(ה)(2)`)'s `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS `the conditions of qualification to serve as an arbitrator appraiser, in a paragraph (2) of a subsection (ה) of section 202`
#ASSERT (`reference: reg 2(ד) of the pay regulations, as printed, to s 202(ה)(2)`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `section 202 of the Law, one paragraph on compensation for the stopping of an exceeding use, with no subsections`

§ `Tests of the day the named text stopped being in force`

-- Defect B. Section 6 of Amendment 116 repeals section 257א; section 16(א) commences the Amendment six months after publication on 25 April 2017. The row types 26 October 2017,
-- the first day certain on either counting (fork F2 in NOTES.md).
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: reg 83(א) of the licensing regulations to s 257א`) (Date 26 10 2017) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: reg 83(א) of the licensing regulations to s 257א`) (Date 27 10 2017) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: reg 83(א) of the licensing regulations to s 257א`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The day before and the earlier days: the row does not say (25 October 2017 is the other possible commencement day; 25 April 2017 is the day of publication).
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: reg 83(א) of the licensing regulations to s 257א`) (Date 25 10 2017) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: reg 83(א) of the licensing regulations to s 257א`) (Date 25 4 2017) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: reg 83(א) of the licensing regulations to s 257א`) (Date 4 7 2016) EQUALS NOTHING
